# This repo is the findings log plus the code that produced it. What is excluded
# is excluded for a reason, not by accident:
#
# upstream repo vendored for study (15 MB, re-fetchable from its own source) -
# kept locally, not carried through history. Note the two directories that ARE
# tracked even though they hold vendor material: pull/ (the original config.sh and
# web pages, i.e. the undo path) and logs/vendor/ (the .so files every ABI claim in
# the README was derived from). Small, and losing them would make the findings
# unreproducible. They are proprietary: do not push this repo anywhere public and
# do not redistribute them.
reference/

# regenerable: tools/package.sh builds it
dist/

# the camera's API token. Never commit it; nothing else in the tree contains it
# (checked with grep -rl before the first commit)
tools/.token
*.token

# cross-compiled build products - rebuild with the armv5 toolchain, and a stale
# akrtsp.stripped is a real deployment hazard here (see README, "Deploying the
# wrong binary")
src/akstream
src/akstream.stripped
src/akrtsp
src/akrtsp.stripped
src/akvi_probe
src/akir_probe
src/akir_probe.stripped
src/irprobe
src/*.o
*.elf

# local relay/browser scratch
__pycache__/
*.pyc
